.docs/plans/_archive/v1.0.0.md:391:| **I575** | Progressive enrichment everywhere | Every AI-powered operation in the app should write partial results as they arrive, not wait for the full response. Applies to all surfaces, not just entity intelligence. **Entity enrichment:** `write_partial_enrichment()` merges one dimension into existing `entity_assessment` without overwriting others. `entity-dimension-updated` Tauri event per write. Account detail page shows dimensions filling in progressively. **Report generation:** sections write as they complete — executive summary appears first, deep dives populate incrementally. Report page shows sections rendering one by one. **Transcript processing:** summary + actions land first, then sentiment + dynamics, then commitments + champion health. Meeting detail page updates as each section arrives. **Email enrichment:** already fast (60s individual), but batch email enrichment should write per-email as each completes instead of waiting for the batch. **Meeting prep:** already mechanical (no PTY), but prep sections that depend on entity intelligence should update when their upstream dimension completes. **Frontend pattern:** unified `useProgressiveData(entityId)` hook that subscribes to Tauri events and triggers section-level re-renders without full page reload. Depends on I574 (parallel calls provide the natural write boundaries). |
.docs/plans/_archive/v1.0.0.md:420:67b. ○ Each dimension/section writes to DB as it completes. Frontend receives granular Tauri events. Account detail shows dimensions filling in. Reports show sections rendering. Meeting detail shows transcript results arriving. User sees progress, not a spinner (I575).
.docs/plans/_archive/v1.0.0.md:429:67k. ○ Refresh button shows completion percentage ("Refreshing… 36%") instead of elapsed seconds ("Refreshing… 36s"). Percentage derived from completed dimensions / total dimensions. Backend emits `enrichment-progress` events with `{ entity_id, completed, total }`. Frontend `useAccountDetail` maps this to a percentage. Each dimension completion bumps the counter (I575).
.docs/plans/_archive/v1.0.0.md:472:| **I572** | Audit log for OAuth token lifecycle | P2 | Token save, refresh, delete, and expiry events in Google and Glean token stores should emit audit records. Currently: auth connect/disconnect logged, but individual token operations are not. |
.docs/plans/_archive/v1.0.0.md:473:| **I573** | Mutex poisoning recovery | P2 | When `audit_log`, `config`, or `db` Mutex poisons (a thread panicked while holding the lock), the resource is permanently unusable for the session. Add recovery: re-create the resource or degrade gracefully instead of returning errors for every subsequent call. |
.docs/plans/_archive/v1.0.0.md:493:83. Token refresh, save, and delete operations emit audit log entries with provider name and outcome (I572).
