.docs/decisions/0114-scoring-unification.md:141:Each composer produces its own band taxonomy — trust uses `likely_current | use_with_caution | needs_verification`, health uses a dimension-specific color coding, future composers will define their own. Bands are not shared; forcing a shared band taxonomy would couple unrelated surfaces to a single scale.
.docs/decisions/0114-scoring-unification.md:143:What **is** shared: a `ConfidenceEvidence` struct that every composer emits alongside its score, consumed uniformly by UI rendering.
.docs/decisions/0114-scoring-unification.md:167:UI surfaces render `ConfidenceEvidence` uniformly: a score, a band, an expandable breakdown, and a list of caveats. Bands differ per composer; the rendering shell is common. This is what [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md) consumes.
.docs/decisions/0114-scoring-unification.md:216:- **UI rendering uniform.** One `ConfidenceEvidence` shape means the product's explanation affordance works identically for trust and health without cross-coupling their semantics.
