.docs/decisions/0120-observability-contract.md:63:The record is **invocation-grained**, not log-grained. Individual log messages within an invocation are child records inheriting `invocation_id` + `span_id`. This produces a tree per invocation that the debug trace surface ([DOS-250](https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-250)) can render directly.
.docs/decisions/0120-observability-contract.md:128:The observability contract honors [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md) masking rules. Specifically:
.docs/decisions/0120-observability-contract.md:135:The distinction: logs carry **the shape of what happened**, not **the content of what happened**. Content lives in the encrypted database with the provenance envelopes and `evaluation_traces`. Debug flows pull content at display time through [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md) renderer, not by reading raw logs.
.docs/decisions/0120-observability-contract.md:146:- Records emit normally but are flagged `mode: "Simulate"`. The debug trace surface renders simulation runs distinctly from production runs.
.docs/decisions/0120-observability-contract.md:160:This ADR defines **how observability data is produced**. [DOS-250](https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-250) defines **how it is rendered** to the developer in-app.
.docs/decisions/0120-observability-contract.md:231:- **Debug trace surface ([DOS-250](https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-250)) has a uniform data source.** Every ability looks the same when rendered in the trace panel. No per-ability debug implementation.
.docs/decisions/0120-observability-contract.md:282:- Changing redaction rules: amendment required; changes how renderers operate.
