     8	
     9	## Context
    10	
    11	[ADR-0114](0114-scoring-unification.md) R1.7 placed `user_feedback_weight` as a canonical scoring factor and referenced a `FeedbackAction` enum with placeholder values `StillTrue | Outdated | WrongSource`. [ADR-0113](0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md) §6 declared the agent trust-ledger updates as "User accepts an agent claim → α += 1 / User contradicts → β += 1" without typing accept vs. contradict.
    12	
    13	The v1.4.0 Claim Feedback and Prompt Granularity Review identified that a 5-point accuracy scale or yes/no boolean cannot drive distinct trust, provenance, and repair behavior. Different user intents require different DB writes:
    14	
    15	- "Wrong account" — subject-fit failure; suppress on this entity; do not punish source.
    16	- "Outdated" — claim true historically; downweight current-state trust; do not retract.
    17	- "Wrong source" — attribution failure; downweight source for this claim_type; keep claim open.
    18	- "Can't verify" — uncertainty; do not punish claim; request corroboration.
    19	
    20	Without typed semantics, feedback collected in v1.4.0 would not be translatable into the trust-compiler updates ADR-0114 specifies. **Trust Compiler ships in v1.4.0 spine; therefore feedback semantics close in v1.4.0 spine.** The 7 open decisions from the Linear review are answered below in §3.
    21	
    22	## Decision
    23	
    24	### 1. The `FeedbackAction` enum (closed)
    25	
    26	```rust
    27	pub enum FeedbackAction {
    28	    /// User confirms the claim is true and current.
    29	    /// → α += 1.0 on agent ledger; user corroboration recorded; trust boost via §4.
    30	    ConfirmCurrent,
    31	
    32	    /// User says the claim was true historically but is no longer current.
    33	    /// → original claim transitions to `superseded`; user-authored absence claim
    34	    ///   is committed at the same field_path; trust on the original downweights
    35	    ///   via the freshness factor, not the source factor; α += 0.5 on the agent
    36	    ///   (the claim was correctly authored once).
    37	    MarkOutdated,
    38	
    39	    /// User says the claim is false.
    40	    /// → claim transitions to `withdrawn`; tombstone written if no remaining
    41	    ///   sources support an alternate value; β += 1.0 on agent ledger; one-shot
    42	    ///   modest source downweight (-0.05) — single mistakes may be misclassification.
    43	    MarkFalse,
    44	
    45	    /// User says the content is true but attached to the wrong subject (account,
    46	    /// project, person, meeting). Carries the corrected subject when the user
    47	    /// supplied one; otherwise null = "not relevant to this entity, don't know
    48	    /// which one is right."
    49	    /// → claim suppressed on the asserted subject (per-subject tombstone);
    50	    ///   subject_evidence flagged for the inference path that produced this
    51	    ///   attachment; β += 0.3 on agent (subject mistake, not truth mistake);
    52	    ///   source reliability NOT downweighted.
    53	    /// → consumes the typed `SubjectRef` from ADR-0105 SubjectAttribution amendment.
    54	    WrongSubject { corrected_to: Option<SubjectRef> },
    55	
    56	    /// User says the cited source does not actually support the claim.
    57	    /// → source attribution downweighted (-0.2) on this source for this claim_type;
    58	    ///   claim remains open if other sources clear the trust floor; transitions
    59	    ///   to `withdrawn` if no remaining sources qualify; β += 0.2 on agent.
    60	    WrongSource { source_index: usize },
    61	
    62	    /// User cannot verify the claim from surfaced evidence.
    63	    /// → no trust delta; claim flagged with `NeedsCorroboration` warning;
    64	    ///   targeted repair job enqueued (per §7); if no corroboration found within
    65	    ///   the corroboration window (default 14 days), claim downweights via
    66	    ///   `lack-of-corroboration`, not user-rejection.
    67	    CannotVerify,
    68	
    69	    /// User says the claim is partly right; submits corrected text.
    70	    /// → user-authored superseding claim is committed at the same field_path;
    71	    ///   original claim transitions to `superseded`; source remains attributed
    72	    ///   to the original; agent ledger gets α += 0.3 if the correction reads as
    73	    ///   refinement (text-overlap heuristic ≥ 0.5) or β += 0.3 if contradiction.
    74	    NeedsNuance { corrected_text: String },
    75	
    76	    /// Render/privacy concern, not a truth concern. The claim should not appear
    77	    /// in this surface (e.g., internal note shown as customer-facing fact).
    78	    /// → surface-specific suppression marker recorded; no claim state change;
    79	    ///   no source penalty; feeds ADR-0108 surface privacy policy.
    80	    SurfaceInappropriate { surface: SurfaceId },
    81	
    82	    /// User says the claim is true but not relevant to this meeting/context.
    83	    /// → context-binding hint recorded against the ability invocation that
