   120	### 4. Trust Compiler integration
   121	
   122	The Trust Compiler (DOS-5) consumes `ClaimFeedback` via the `user_feedback_weight` factor (per ADR-0114 R1.3, the factor takes pre-computed `age_days`, not a clock). Per-action deltas:
   123	
   124	| Action | Source weight Δ | Agent ledger Δ | Claim state | Freshness Δ | Subject evidence Δ |
   125	|---|---|---|---|---|---|
   126	| `ConfirmCurrent` | +0.10 (capped) | α += 1.0 | unchanged | refreshed | unchanged |
   127	| `MarkOutdated` | none | α += 0.5 | → `superseded` | downweight to historical | unchanged |
   128	| `MarkFalse` | -0.05 (one-shot) | β += 1.0 | → `withdrawn` | n/a | unchanged |
   129	| `WrongSubject` | none | β += 0.3 | → tombstoned at this subject | unchanged | -0.3 on the inference method that produced this attachment |
   130	| `WrongSource` | -0.20 on cited source for this claim_type | β += 0.2 | unchanged unless no sources remain qualified | unchanged | unchanged |
   131	| `CannotVerify` | none | none | unchanged | unchanged | unchanged; triggers repair |
   132	| `NeedsNuance` | none | α += 0.3 (refinement) or β += 0.3 (contradiction) by text-overlap heuristic ≥ 0.5 | original → `superseded`; new claim committed | refreshed on new claim | inherits |
   133	| `SurfaceInappropriate` | none | none | unchanged | unchanged | unchanged; surface-policy update |
   134	| `NotRelevantHere` | none | none | unchanged | unchanged | unchanged; relevance signal feeds DOS-216 eval |
   135	
   136	These deltas are the spine. **Tuning happens in v1.4.1** against shadow data; the `agent_trust_ledger` and source-weight tables are designed to recompute, so retroactive tuning is safe.
   137	
   138	### 5. Substrate-shaping consequences
   139	
   140	- `scoring::factors::user_feedback_weight(feedback: Option<&UserFeedbackInput>)` (ADR-0114 R1.3) consumes a `UserFeedbackInput { action: FeedbackAction, age_days: f64 }`. Pure; the extractor pulls latest feedback per claim per ADR-0114 §2.
   141	- ADR-0113 §6 agent-ledger updates are typed by `FeedbackAction` rather than abstract "accept/contradict" — see §4.
   142	- ADR-0113 §5 tombstone behavior is now triggered by `WrongSubject` (per-subject tombstone) and `MarkFalse` (broad tombstone), not by an untyped UI gesture.
   143	- DOS-294 ships the `FeedbackAction` enum + `ClaimFeedback` row + service functions (`propose_feedback`, `apply_feedback_to_trust`).
   144	- DOS-8 inline UI uses the typed enum directly. No more untyped `feedback_yes/no/wrong_source` handlers.
   145	
   146	### 6. Subject correction interplay (ADR-0105 amendment)
   147	
   148	`WrongSubject { corrected_to }` is the user-side complement to ADR-0105's `SubjectAttribution` substrate primitive. Behavior:
   149	
   150	- `corrected_to: None` — "this content does not belong to this entity; I don't know whose it is." Tombstone the claim at the asserted subject only; do not propose a new attachment.
   151	- `corrected_to: Some(SubjectRef)` — "this content belongs to that entity instead." Tombstone at the asserted subject; propose (not commit) a new claim at the corrected subject with the same claim_text, full provenance preserved, `actor = 'user_correction'`. The corrected claim enters via the standard propose/commit path so it gets the same gate as any other claim.
   152	
   153	The inference method that produced the wrong attachment receives `subject_evidence` downweight `-0.3`. After repeated `WrongSubject` feedback against the same `InferenceMethod` for the same source class, the inference method gets globally suppressed for that source class (threshold: 5 instances within 30 days).
   154	
   155	### 7. Repair scheduling for `CannotVerify`
   156	
   157	When `CannotVerify` is recorded:
   158	
   159	1. A `claim_repair_job` row is enqueued via DOS-236 invalidation queue with `priority = normal`.
   160	2. Job retrieves up to 10 candidate corroborating sources via Glean + local context.
   161	3. Job invokes a `find_corroborating_evidence` Read ability (lands in v1.4.1; v1.4.0 ships the queue + skeleton).
   162	4. Found corroboration → claim corroboration record (ADR-0113 R1.6); user notified.
   163	5. No corroboration within 14 days → claim downweights via `lack-of-corroboration` factor; lint surface flags it.
   164	
   165	Budgets: 1 LLM call + 1 retrieval batch per job; max 5 active repair jobs per entity; max 50 per workspace. Excess queues at `priority = low`.
   166	
   167	### 8. Non-goals for v1.4.0
   168	
   169	- UI surfaces beyond DOS-8's inline six. Overflow menu (`NeedsNuance` editor, `SurfaceInappropriate`, `NotRelevantHere`), claim detail panel, lint feedback debt — v1.4.2.
   170	- Cross-claim feedback aggregation ("user often marks Glean Salesforce sources wrong" → systematic source downweight). Tracked separately for v1.5.0+.
   171	- Feedback from non-User actors. Enum supports `created_by: ClaimActor` for future agent-to-agent feedback; v1.4.0 commits user-only.
